From 9eee9c59dd9961e2c5befe4a4a597681863044cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sn3ro <zak.darek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:48:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): a 3+2 first-traverse refusal names the heights the
 user set

The first-traverse law reads a 3+2 path in its tilted frame, where
generate shifted each height by h - origin.z. The refusal named those
local values: a clearance height of 30 read as Z10.000.

operation::first_traverse::judge now adds origin.z back to the two
heights of the verdict and sets the new field
Warning::FirstTraverseLow::tilted (serde default false, so an old
cache loads as upright) when the frame is not upright. A tilted verdict
says that the heights are measured along the tilted tool axis and
names the raise, with no Z value and no X/Y. The upright text does not
change. The troubleshooting page and the indexed guide page describe
the new text.

Pinned by first_traverse::a_3_2_plane_reads_the_stock_top_along_its_tool_axis,
verify::first_traverse::tests::a_tilted_verdict_names_the_raise_not_a_z_value
and verify::first_traverse::tests::a_verdict_saved_before_tilted_reads_as_upright.

Fixes #2991

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
